{"id":"coding-loops","title":"Coding: loops","subject":"Coding","label":"Coding","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":177,"duration":177.24,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":506,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Everyday puzzle","start":0,"end":17.445},{"id":"explain","title":"Repeat work","start":17.445,"end":49.515},{"id":"explain2","title":"While loops","start":49.515,"end":73.305},{"id":"example","title":"Worked sum","start":73.305,"end":104.405},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":104.405,"end":116.145},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":116.145,"end":123.385},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":123.385,"end":147.925},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":147.925,"end":177.24}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":5.99,"text":"Have you ever copied the same line of code again and again? I'm Kora. Loops solve that.","w":[0.52,0.66,0.92,1.18,1.56,1.68,1.94,2.16,2.26,2.52,2.78,2.9,3.78,4.02,4.9,5.28,5.64]},{"s":0,"a":6.29,"b":9.52,"text":"They let one small block of code do repeated work for you.","w":[6.36,6.54,6.9,7.12,7.44,7.76,7.88,8.22,8.42,8.86,9.1,9.26]},{"s":0,"a":9.82,"b":14.57,"text":"Today you'll see exactly how they repeat work, and how to stop them going forever.","w":[9.86,10.26,10.5,10.7,11.3,11.46,11.62,11.98,12.78,12.96,13.16,13.28,13.58,13.76,14.14]},{"s":0,"a":14.87,"b":17.02,"text":"That saves time and prevents mistakes.","w":[14.9,15.12,15.44,15.82,15.94,16.38]},{"s":1,"a":17.87,"b":21.55,"text":"A loop repeats a block of code, so you do not copy and paste.","w":[17.92,18.02,18.32,18.74,18.84,19.16,19.3,19.94,20.12,20.26,20.4,20.64,21.02,21.14]},{"s":1,"a":21.85,"b":24.16,"text":"The repeated block is called the loop body.","w":[21.88,22.02,22.5,22.94,23.06,23.36,23.5,23.8]},{"s":1,"a":24.46,"b":29.25,"text":"A for loop repeats once for each item in a sequence, or a set number of times.","w":[24.52,24.62,24.8,25.04,25.66,25.94,26.18,26.5,26.8,26.9,26.98,27.92,28.06,28.16,28.4,28.68,28.78]},{"s":1,"a":29.55,"b":31.45,"text":"A sequence could be a list of names.","w":[29.6,29.7,30.16,30.32,30.46,30.56,30.82,30.94]},{"s":1,"a":31.75,"b":34.57,"text":"A set number of times is useful when you know the count.","w":[31.82,31.96,32.24,32.5,32.62,33.06,33.26,33.62,33.76,33.9,34.06,34.16]},{"s":1,"a":34.87,"b":38.55,"text":"In Python, for i in range of five runs five times.","w":[34.92,35.04,35.94,36.28,36.52,36.66,36.96,37.1,37.44,37.84,38.12]},{"s":1,"a":38.85,"b":42.99,"text":"Here i goes zero, one, two, three, four, because counting starts at zero.","w":[38.9,39.12,39.22,39.72,40.18,40.34,40.56,40.82,41.56,41.84,42.2,42.52,42.6]},{"s":1,"a":43.29,"b":46.81,"text":"So the first pass uses zero, and the last pass uses four.","w":[43.36,43.52,43.66,43.96,44.32,44.56,45.34,45.44,45.56,45.88,46.22,46.48]},{"s":1,"a":47.11,"b":49.09,"text":"Each pass is called an iteration.","w":[47.2,47.42,48,48.12,48.4,48.54]},{"s":2,"a":49.94,"b":53.02,"text":"A while loop repeats as long as a condition stays true.","w":[50.02,50.14,50.52,50.78,51.36,51.52,51.78,51.9,51.96,52.42,52.72]},{"s":2,"a":53.32,"b":56.14,"text":"A condition is a test that is either true or false.","w":[53.4,53.48,53.98,54.12,54.2,54.48,54.66,54.8,55.08,55.52,55.68]},{"s":2,"a":56.44,"b":60.76,"text":"Something inside the loop must change, or the condition never becomes false.","w":[56.56,56.9,57.26,57.4,57.74,58.02,58.84,58.96,59.08,59.66,59.92,60.28]},{"s":2,"a":61.06,"b":63.74,"text":"If it never changes, the loop keeps running.","w":[61.14,61.28,61.42,61.72,62.6,62.76,63.06,63.38]},{"s":2,"a":64.04,"b":66.78,"text":"Then it never stops. That is an infinite loop.","w":[64.04,64.24,64.4,64.7,65.48,65.72,65.84,66.04,66.44]},{"s":2,"a":67.08,"b":69.18,"text":"Plan what changes before you write the loop.","w":[67.12,67.52,67.74,68.12,68.42,68.54,68.76,68.86]},{"s":2,"a":69.48,"b":72.88,"text":"A variable that adds things up across the loop is an accumulator.","w":[69.56,69.7,70.22,70.54,70.76,71.1,71.24,71.62,71.74,72.1,72.2,72.28]},{"s":3,"a":73.73,"b":77.17,"text":"Let's add the numbers one to five. total starts at zero.","w":[73.76,74.02,74.18,74.3,74.76,74.92,75.04,75.76,76.14,76.64,76.78]},{"s":3,"a":77.47,"b":82.06,"text":"For each number from one to five, total equals total plus number.","w":[77.47,77.72,77.96,78.28,78.6,78.8,78.96,79.72,80.1,80.9,81.44,81.74]},{"s":3,"a":82.36,"b":84.5,"text":"The board shows the real Python code.","w":[82.44,82.6,82.92,83.24,83.4,83.7,84.16]},{"s":3,"a":84.8,"b":86.61,"text":"Watch total grow step by step.","w":[84.84,85.2,85.58,85.92,86.16,86.34]},{"s":3,"a":86.91,"b":91.25,"text":"After one, total is one. After two, total is three.","w":[87.02,87.42,88.08,88.5,88.76,89.46,89.76,90.48,90.84,90.96]},{"s":3,"a":91.55,"b":95.65,"text":"After three, total is six. After four, total is ten.","w":[91.64,91.94,92.6,93.06,93.24,93.82,94.12,94.74,95.1,95.24]},{"s":3,"a":95.95,"b":100.13,"text":"After five, total is fifteen. So the loop ends with fifteen.","w":[96.04,96.34,97,97.44,97.6,98.6,98.76,98.88,99.24,99.46,99.66]},{"s":3,"a":100.43,"b":103.98,"text":"This pattern is an accumulator. total gathers the running sum.","w":[100.48,100.72,101.1,101.22,101.3,101.98,102.76,103.18,103.32,103.66]},{"s":4,"a":104.83,"b":105.48,"text":"Quick check.","w":[104.88,105.12]},{"s":4,"a":105.78,"b":110.22,"text":"How many times does for i in range of three run, and what values does i take?","w":[105.84,106.04,106.28,106.6,106.8,107.12,107.34,107.46,107.74,107.86,108.18,108.88,109.02,109.24,109.66,109.9,110]},{"s":4,"a":110.67,"b":113.49,"text":"Say the number of runs first, then the values.","w":[110.78,110.98,111.12,111.4,111.54,111.86,112.62,112.84,112.96]},{"s":4,"a":113.79,"b":115.72,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[113.8,114.18,114.44,114.54,114.82,115.22,115.4]},{"s":5,"a":116.57,"b":121.54,"text":"Three times. i takes zero, one, and two, because range starts counting at zero.","w":[116.6,116.84,117.76,117.86,118.12,118.78,118.92,119.06,119.64,119.98,120.36,120.68,121.06,121.16]},{"s":5,"a":121.84,"b":122.96,"text":"It never reaches three.","w":[121.88,122.04,122.36,122.74]},{"s":6,"a":123.81,"b":129.29,"text":"One common mistake is an off by one error, like expecting range of five to include five.","w":[124,124.2,124.56,125.1,125.22,125.42,125.64,125.92,126.14,126.84,127.08,127.62,127.92,128.04,128.42,128.56,128.94]},{"s":6,"a":129.59,"b":132.55,"text":"Avoid it by checking where counting starts and stops.","w":[129.66,130.1,130.24,130.46,130.82,131.06,131.46,131.94,132.08]},{"s":6,"a":132.85,"b":137.75,"text":"Another is forgetting to update the variable in a while loop, which can create an infinite loop.","w":[132.96,133.42,133.56,133.98,134.16,134.48,134.6,135.08,135.18,135.26,135.56,136.04,136.24,136.44,136.84,137.02,137.4]},{"s":6,"a":138.05,"b":140.27,"text":"Also check you change the right variable.","w":[138.16,138.7,138.94,139.12,139.42,139.54,139.74]},{"s":6,"a":140.57,"b":144.54,"text":"And put lines after the loop when they should run once, not inside it.","w":[140.6,140.76,141.02,141.4,141.62,141.72,142.36,142.52,142.66,142.86,143.16,143.76,144.02,144.44]},{"s":6,"a":144.84,"b":147.5,"text":"Trace small loops by hand to see each iteration.","w":[144.88,145.24,145.56,145.84,146.04,146.34,146.46,146.7,146.94]},{"s":7,"a":148.35,"b":152.25,"text":"Recap. A loop repeats code so you do not copy and paste.","w":[148.4,149.18,149.3,149.62,150.08,150.7,150.86,151,151.14,151.34,151.68,151.8]},{"s":7,"a":152.55,"b":155.96,"text":"A for loop repeats for each item or a set number of times.","w":[152.64,152.74,152.96,153.24,153.68,153.88,154.18,154.56,154.7,154.82,155.06,155.32,155.42]},{"s":7,"a":156.26,"b":161.11,"text":"A while loop repeats while a condition stays true, so update something inside it.","w":[156.34,156.44,156.76,157.04,157.64,157.86,157.92,158.4,158.74,159.52,159.86,160.28,160.62,161]},{"s":7,"a":161.41,"b":165.96,"text":"Each pass is one iteration, and an accumulator adds things up across the loop.","w":[161.5,161.78,162.14,162.36,162.5,163.46,163.6,163.7,164.54,164.78,165.12,165.28,165.64,165.74]},{"s":7,"a":166.26,"b":169.38,"text":"Check the starting value, the condition, and the update.","w":[166.3,166.58,166.74,167.14,167.9,168.02,168.76,168.9,169.06]},{"s":7,"a":169.68,"b":172.87,"text":"Top tip: trace your loop by hand with small numbers.","w":[169.7,170.02,170.68,170.98,171.14,171.38,171.56,171.88,172.08,172.38]},{"s":7,"a":173.17,"b":176.64,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and you'll spot loops quickly.","w":[173.22,173.52,174.12,174.3,175.24,175.36,175.6,175.94,176.24]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Everyday puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Copying the same code again and again?"},{"at":6.19,"kind":"text","text":"Loops do repeated work for you."},{"at":9.72,"kind":"text","text":"How loops repeat, and how to stop endless ones"},{"at":14.77,"kind":"text","text":"Saves time; prevents mistakes."}]},{"at":17.62,"heading":"Loops","items":[{"at":17.77,"kind":"term","text":"Loop","detail":"Repeats a block of code; no copy-paste"},{"at":21.75,"kind":"term","text":"Loop body","detail":"The repeated block of code"},{"at":24.36,"kind":"term","text":"for loop","detail":"Repeats for each item or a set number of times"},{"at":29.45,"kind":"term","text":"Sequence","detail":"e.g. a list of names"},{"at":31.65,"kind":"text","text":"Set number of times: when count is known"}]},{"at":34.62,"heading":"Python for loop","items":[{"at":34.77,"kind":"formula","text":"for i in range(5):"},{"at":34.77,"kind":"text","text":"runs 5 times"},{"at":38.75,"kind":"text","text":"i = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4"},{"at":43.19,"kind":"text","text":"First pass i = 0; last pass i = 4"},{"at":47.01,"kind":"term","text":"Iteration","detail":"Each pass through the loop"}]},{"at":49.69,"heading":"While loops","items":[{"at":49.84,"kind":"term","text":"while loop","detail":"Repeats while a condition stays true"},{"at":53.22,"kind":"term","text":"Condition","detail":"A test that is true or false"},{"at":56.34,"kind":"text","text":"Something inside must change."},{"at":60.96,"kind":"text","text":"If it never changes, loop keeps running."},{"at":63.94,"kind":"term","text":"Infinite loop","detail":"A loop that never stops"}]},{"at":66.83,"heading":"Plan & accumulate","items":[{"at":66.98,"kind":"text","text":"Plan what changes before you write."},{"at":69.38,"kind":"term","text":"Accumulator","detail":"Adds things up across the loop"}]},{"at":73.48,"heading":"Worked sum: code","items":[{"at":73.63,"kind":"formula","text":"total = 0"},{"at":77.37,"kind":"formula","text":"for n in range(1, 6):"},{"at":82.26,"kind":"formula","text":"    total = total + n"},{"at":82.26,"kind":"text","text":"range(1, 6) gives 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 (stops before 6)"}]},{"at":84.55,"heading":"Running total","items":[{"at":84.7,"kind":"text","text":"Watch total grow step by step."},{"at":86.81,"kind":"step","text":"n = 1: total 1; n = 2: total 3"},{"at":91.45,"kind":"step","text":"n = 3: total 6; n = 4: total 10"},{"at":95.85,"kind":"step","text":"n = 5: total 15"},{"at":100.33,"kind":"term","text":"Accumulator","detail":"total gathers the running sum"}]},{"at":104.41,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":104.41,"kind":"question","text":"How many times does for i in range(3) run, and what values does i take?"}]},{"at":116.32,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":116.47,"kind":"text","text":"3 times; i = 0, 1, 2"},{"at":121.74,"kind":"text","text":"range stops before 3."}]},{"at":123.56,"heading":"Off-by-one","items":[{"at":123.71,"kind":"wrong","text":"Expect range(5) to include 5"},{"at":123.71,"kind":"right","text":"range(5) gives i = 0–4"},{"at":129.49,"kind":"text","text":"Check where counting starts and stops."}]},{"at":132.6,"heading":"Loop mistakes","items":[{"at":132.75,"kind":"wrong","text":"Forget to update while variable"},{"at":132.75,"kind":"right","text":"Update the variable inside the loop"},{"at":137.95,"kind":"text","text":"Change the right variable."},{"at":140.47,"kind":"text","text":"Put once-only lines after the loop."},{"at":144.74,"kind":"tip","text":"Trace small loops by hand to see each iteration."}]},{"at":148.1,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":148.25,"kind":"text","text":"Loop repeats code; no copy-paste."},{"at":152.45,"kind":"text","text":"for: each item or set number of times."},{"at":156.16,"kind":"text","text":"while: while condition true; update inside."},{"at":161.31,"kind":"text","text":"Iteration = one pass; accumulator adds up."},{"at":166.16,"kind":"text","text":"Check start value, condition, update."}]},{"at":169.43,"heading":"Top tip","items":[{"at":169.58,"kind":"tip","text":"Trace your loop by hand with small numbers."},{"at":173.07,"kind":"text","text":"Practise with Knowzone."}]}],"check":{"at":115.97,"seconds":10,"question":"How many times does for i in range(3) run, and what values does i take?","answer":"3 times; i = 0, 1, 2. range stops before 3."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}